## 1. THE SOCIAL ARBITRAGE PHILOSOPHY

### 1.1 Core Principle

**Intentionally ignore Wall Street.** No fundamental analysis, no P/E ratios, no technical charts.

The entire philosophy: **Detect real-world shifts in culture, consumer behavior, or technology faster than the market, and connect those dots to investable opportunities.**

### 1.2 What He Does NOT Do

| Method | Reason for Rejection |
|--------|---------------------|
| Fundamental analysis (P/E, DCF, etc.) | Lagging — by the time it shows up, the market has already moved |
| Technical charts / stock price | "Trades blind to stock price" — the information is the edge, not the price |
| Wall Street analyst reports | Always late — consensus is already priced in |
| Macroeconomic forecasts | Impossible to predict; distracts from micro-trends |
| Financial media (CNBC, WSJ) | "Poison" — filled with noise and consensus groupthink |

