## 2. OBSERVATION & DATA GATHERING

### 2.1 Primary Data Sources

| Source | How Used | Why Valuable |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| **TikTok comments** | 4 hours late-night reading thousands of raw comments | Most raw, transparent consumer expression — users show buying intent before purchase |
| **Google Trends** | Search volume tracking | Quantifies interest trajectory before it hits sales data |
| **Website checkout traffic** | Paid traffic data for specific ticketing/sales pages | Confirms that conversation is converting to purchases |
| **Reddit forums** | Niche community discussion tracking | Early signal on emerging trends |
| **Real-world channel checks** | Talk to store clerks and managers | "Infiltrate" physical retail — unfiltered sales data |

### 2.2 The TikTok Edge

Camillo believes **TikTok is the absolute gold standard for alpha** because:
- Users are deeply raw, emotional, and transparent about buying intentions
- It's the only major platform not yet dominated by politics and finance chatter
- Comments reveal real passion: "obsessed," "sold out everywhere," "need this"

### 2.3 The Platform Evolution

| Era | Primary Source | Why It Changed |
|-----|---------------|----------------|
| **Pre-2010** | Walking malls, observing restaurant lines, Yahoo message boards | Only sources available |
| **Early 2010s** | Twitter (X) — built TickerTags analyzing 10% of the Twitter firehose | Twitter users talked about products and movies |
| **Late 2010s** | Twitter declining in value | Users pivoted to politics and news — stopped talking about everyday products |
| **Current** | **TikTok** | Only platform with raw consumer intent data |

