## 3. THE FILTERING FUNNEL

### 3.1 The Funnel

Camillo starts with a massive funnel of ideas but executes only **4 to 8 trades per year**.

### 3.2 Must-Pass Criteria

| Criterion | What It Means |
|-----------|---------------|
| **The Needle Mover Test** | The trend must be significant enough to meaningfully impact a company's revenue, cost structure, or public perception |
| **No Offsetting Catalysts** | No hidden, unrelated failures within the company that could wipe out the trend's gains |
| **Off-Radar** | The trend must not yet be appreciated by institutional Wall Street or general investing public |
| **AI-Assisted Revenue Exposure** | Use LLMs to calculate what % of revenue the trending product represents for each company |

```mermaid
graph TD
    FUNNEL[Massive Funnel: Hundreds of Observations] --> NM{The Needle Mover Test}
    NM -->|Yes| OC{No Offsetting Catalysts}
    NM -->|No| DISCARD[Discard]
    OC -->|Yes| OR{Off-Radar? Not Yet Discovered by Wall Street}
    OC -->|No| DISCARD
    OR -->|Yes| AI[AI-Assisted Revenue Exposure Calculation]
    OR -->|No| DISCARD
    AI --> CONVICTION{High Enough Conviction?}
    CONVICTION -->|Yes - 4 to 8 per Year| ENTER[Enter: Information Asymmetry]
    CONVICTION -->|No| WAIT[Wait / Watch]
    style ENTER fill:#1a4a1a,color:#fff
    style DISCARD fill:#4a1a1a,color:#fff
```

### 3.3 The Needle Mover Test in Detail

**Must verify** that the cultural shift is large enough to violently disrupt:
- Overall revenue
- Cost structure
- Public perception

**Common failure:** Finding a hot product at a giant company where the product is <1% of revenue.

### 3.4 The Offsetting Catalyst Check

**Must aggressively search** for hidden, unrelated failures:
- Check every division of the company (not just the one with the trend)
- Look for franchisee revolts, management scandals, regulatory issues
- A great product trend will NOT save a company with a fatal structural problem elsewhere

