## 11. AI WORKFLOW & AGENTS

### 11.1 The Core AI Workflow

When Camillo spots a cultural shift (e.g., "denim skirts are coming back"):

1. **Prompt** ChatGPT Pro or Claude (Opus) to map the supply chain
2. **Ask AI** to identify every publicly traded company that touches the trend
3. **Calculate** revenue exposure percentage for each company
4. **Apply human judgment** — AI does "dirty work research," Camillo provides conviction

### 11.2 The Surrender Prompt

His foundational prompt strategy:

> *"Ask me anything you need to ask me so that we can do this in the best way possible."*

Or:

> *"I don't even know what I should be asking you right now, so can you please ask me anything you need so we can get started on this journey?"*

This surrenders control to the AI to guide the research direction.

### 11.3 Autonomous AI Agents

His community built agents using frameworks like **OpenClaw on Mac Minis** that:
- Watch TikTok videos 24 hours a day
- Scrape comment sections
- Identify trigger words: **"obsessed," "sold out everywhere"**
- Map trends to publicly traded companies
- Suggest trades

**Current status:** Agents are "brilliant dirty work research assistants" but still lack human intuition for cultural nuance. Camillo validates every suggestion.

### 11.4 AI Guardrails

- **Never** asks AI blindly what stocks to buy
- Uses AI purely for research acceleration
- Applies own human conviction to pull the trigger

