## 13. PSYCHOLOGY & EMOTIONAL CONTROL

### 13.1 The Emotional Framework

**Core operating mode:** "Probabilities and outcomes."

Willing to take a 30% portfolio position in options if there is a 50% chance of a 4x-10x return against a low probability of total loss.

### 13.2 Surviving Devastating Losses

| Stage | Action |
|-------|--------|
| **The loss** | "Sleep it off for two days" — literally |
| **Post-loss analysis** | Meticulously dissect the missing variable |
| **Recovery** | Regain composure → aggressively re-leverage on next high-conviction thesis |
| **Key enabler** | Big money account — treating capital as "other people's money" removes fear |

### 13.3 Post-Win Discipline

**The danger:** "After a grand slam, traders become blindly overconfident and make the worst trades of their lives."

**The rule:** **"Do less."** Physically walk away from the market after a massive win. Take a break.

### 13.4 24-Hour Market Cleanses

Camillo advocates for taking **24-hour market cleanses** — literally refusing to look at any financial news or tickers for a full day every month. This resets the nervous system.

### 13.5 The Ultimate Goal

> *"Peaceful dopamine" — not an endlessly growing bank account, but the joy of having coffee with your dog and walking your neighborhood."

