## 15. THE 20-CRITERIA INVESTMENT RUBRIC

### Scoring Scale

| Level | Label | Description |
|-------|-------|-------------|
| **1** | Wall Street Traditionalist | Relies on lagging metrics, financial media, and consensus |
| **2** | Novice Observer | Recognizes real-world trends but lacks discipline |
| **3** | Competent Arb Trader | Executes on trends but misses deep validation or risk bucketing |
| **4** | Advanced Social Arbitrageur | Highly skilled, fast execution, leverages AI and community |
| **5** | Camillo Mastery | Perfect execution with extreme conviction, leverage, emotional control |

### I. Data & Research

| # | Criterion | Level 1 | Level 3 | Level 5 |
|---|-----------|---------|---------|---------|
| 1 | **Primary Data Source** | Lagging transactional data (credit card swipes, SEC filings) | Active on social media but focuses on stock tickers | Spends 4 hours nightly analyzing raw TikTok comments for buying intent |
| 2 | **Valuation & Fundamentals** | Obsesses over P/E ratios and spreadsheets | Uses fundamentals as primary filter before social catalyst | Trades entirely blind to stock price — ignores charts and fundamentals |
| 3 | **Trade Entry** | After major news reports a breakthrough | Attempts early entry but hesitates waiting for price validation | Executes aggressively at exact moment of information asymmetry |
| 4 | **Trade Exit** | Based on predefined fundamental price target | Exits slowly after earnings reports validate thesis | Exits exactly at information parity — when hedge funds/media catch up |
| 5 | **AI Integration** | Refuses to use AI | Uses AI to summarize news articles | Deploys LLMs to map supply chains and calculate revenue exposure instantly |

### II. The Filtering Funnel

| # | Criterion | Level 1 | Level 3 | Level 5 |
|---|-----------|---------|---------|---------|
| 6 | **The Needle Mover Test** | Buys stock because company was mentioned in viral video | Analyzes product sales but doesn't calculate % of total revenue | Meticulously verifies trend will violently disrupt revenue, costs, or perception |
| 7 | **Offsetting Catalysts** | Ignores broader company operations | Briefly checks recent earnings for bad news | Aggressively searches for hidden failures across every division |
| 8 | **Handling Market Noise** | Watches CNBC, panics over Fed rate hikes | Consumes finance media but filters some panic | Cuts out broadcast news entirely — pure independent observation |
| 9 | **Idea Filtering** | Day trades dozens of stocks daily | Tracks trends but lacks patience for perfect alignment | 4-8 highly-vetted "game-changer" trades per year from massive research funnel |
| 10 | **Cross-Validation** | Buys because one influencer mentioned it | Checks Google Trends but doesn't verify conversions | Corroborates conversational data + Google Trends + checkout traffic + credit card data |

### III. Execution & Psychology

| # | Criterion | Level 1 | Level 3 | Level 5 |
